        <activityName xml:lang="en">Acetic acid, 98% in H2O, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Acetic acid, 98% in H2O, at plant
Theoretical data from process analysis. Only the most important flows are taken into account. Energy demand is calculated.;
CAS number: 000064-19-7; 
Formula: C2H4O2; 
Synonyms: Ethansäure; 
UUID: 095a7896-a301-3b3d-bebc-f0ebaae53326
production including refining.
Location: undefined
Technology: The process stands for the Monsanto process in which methanol reacts with carbon monoxide under the influence of a rhodium catalyst. It is assumed that 50% of the off-gas is burned as fuel, thus VOC emissions are reduced and CO2 is higher.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: theoretical model 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_095a7896-a301-3b3d-bebc-f0ebaae53326.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
